nodecode-song-gift is a rewrite of GptsApp's GptsApp/custom-song-gift-mcp:

  https://github.com/GptsApp/custom-song-gift-mcp
  commit 2b436a21a5b68422cc009633e56dd3aa244b453e
  MIT, Copyright (c) Custom Song Gift (declared in plugin.json)

The plugin was a declarative package: a plugin.json with the ChatGPT app
interface block and a per-tool review, an mcp.json naming the hosted MCP
server https://customsonggift.org/api/mcp with no authentication, and one
skill file describing the occasions and styles. It held no code at all. This
rewrite keeps the server's four read-only tools by their own names --
list_occasions, list_styles, guide_story_and_lyrics and get_pricing_options
-- at the same endpoint, and speaks MCP's streamable HTTP to that endpoint
itself through nlk:http (one initialize, then the tool), so no MCP transport,
no Hermes runtime and no manifest are needed. Because the server serves its
own schema at runtime and the pinned commit carries no copy of it, each tool
declares the members worth naming, sends only what a call filled in, and
carries an "extra" object that passes any argument of the server's own tool
through unchanged. The skill's guidance and the manifest's description are
the cell's manual topic, (help :song-gift), and the operator's command is
/song-gift. The interface block is left out: display name, brand colours,
composer icon and sample prompts are app-store metadata, and a cell has its
own listing. Nothing of the original is vendored.
